---
/**
 * The proofs section: what Bend's checker proves about this BLAKE3, against
 * what the official crate's tests check. The laws come from bend/LAWS.bend
 * (src/lib/proofs.ts); the gate's time comes from results.json.
 */
import Section from './Section.astro';
import { adr } from '../lib/adr';
import { results } from '../lib/results';
import { GENERATOR_URL, LAWS_URL, PROOF_URL, lawCount, lawGroups, lemmaCount, sample, type Scope } from '../lib/proofs';
import { blobUrl } from '../lib/site';
import { machineName } from '../lib/page';

const gate = results.proofs;
const minutes = gate ? Math.round(gate.seconds / 60) : undefined;
const shown = sample('ob.hash');

// "2^6,275" -> 2 with a superscript, as text and <sup> parts.
const powers = (text: string) => text.split(/\^([\d,]+|[a-z])/);

const badge: Record<Scope, string> = {
  'every-input': '∀ input',
  'every-size': '∀ size',
  computed: 'computed',
};

// What the official crate's own tests (src/test.rs) check, beside the laws.
const contrast = [
  {
    what: 'The SIMD compression',
    rust: 'Each backend against the portable code on one 61-byte block, one counter and one set of flags.',
    bend: 'Each of compress8’s eight lanes against the scalar compression, for every block, CV, counter and flag set.',
    laws: ['compress8.lane'],
  },
  {
    what: 'Many parents at once',
    rust: 'hash_many over 31 chunks and 31 parents, at three starting counters.',
    bend: 'par8 against eight scalar parents, for every pair of 8-lane CVs.',
    laws: ['par8.lane'],
  },
  {
    what: 'The tree',
    rust: '39 input lengths up to 100 KiB against the reference implementation, and 10,000 seeded random inputs up to 4 KiB.',
    bend: 'Every chunk count: the 1 GiB segment split, the GPU-style reduction, leaf and parent counts, and the streaming stack.',
    laws: ['segments', 'levels', 'tree.leaves', 'stream.shape'],
  },
];

const limits = [
  'The code passes Array.fork, which is @unsafe in Base; the laws pass Array.clone. share.fork proves the laws’ copy is Array.fork’s own body, (a, a); that the runtime may share one buffer for it is trusted.',
  'The compression function itself is pinned by the official vectors and the message-schedule law. There is no second description of BLAKE3’s compression in Bend to prove it against.',
  'Streaming and a big file’s parts: b3io.bend imports the effects and Array.fork, so the stream laws are about a model of its merge stack (Nat counts, no ROOT flag), and how the loader cuts a file into parts is the loader’s.',
  'Outside Bend: the C that moves bytes (effs/load.c, effs/emit.c, the library’s hook), the native Metal and CUDA kernels, the CPU + GPU split (bench code), and Bend’s compiler, runtime and checker.',
];
---

<Section id="proofs" kicker="Under the hood · machine-checked" title="Proven for every input, not only tested">
  <Fragment slot="lede">
    <p>
      Bend’s type checker is also a prover. A <code>law</code> in <a href={LAWS_URL}>LAWS.bend</a> states a claim; a def of the same name in{' '}
      <a href={PROOF_URL}>PROOF.bend</a> proves it; <code>bend PROOF.bend</code> prints <strong>ALL PROOFS CHECK</strong> only when every law holds. The Rust
      compiler checks types and lifetimes, but a claim like “lane 3 equals the scalar compression for every input” is not something Rust can state, let alone
      check. The official crate’s evidence is tests, on inputs someone picked.
    </p>
  </Fragment>

  <ul class="stats" role="list">
    <li class="card" data-reveal style="--i: 0">
      <span class="stat">{lawCount}</span>
      <span class="stat-label">laws about this BLAKE3, all proven</span>
    </li>
    <li class="card" data-reveal style="--i: 1">
      <span class="stat">{lemmaCount}</span>
      <span class="stat-label">lemmas proven on the way</span>
    </li>
    <li class="card" data-reveal style="--i: 2">
      <span class="stat">0</span>
      <span class="stat-label">open claims, and no <code>@unsafe</code> code under the laws</span>
    </li>
    {
      minutes !== undefined && (
        <li class="card" data-reveal style="--i: 3">
          <span class="stat">~{minutes} min</span>
          <span class="stat-label">for <code>bend/prove.sh</code> on the {machineName}</span>
        </li>
      )
    }
  </ul>

  <div class="contrast card" data-reveal>
    <table>
      <caption class="sr-only">What the official Rust crate’s tests check, beside what this port’s laws prove</caption>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col"><span class="sr-only">Part</span></th>
          <th scope="col">Official Rust crate: tested</th>
          <th scope="col">Bend2 port: proven</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          contrast.map((c) => (
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">{c.what}</th>
              <td class="rust">{c.rust}</td>
              <td class="bend">
                {c.bend} <span class="law-refs">{c.laws.map((n) => <code>{n}</code>)}</span>
              </td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p class="aside prose">
    The Rust column is the official crate’s <a href="https://github.com/BLAKE3-team/BLAKE3/blob/master/src/test.rs">src/test.rs</a>. This port runs tests
    too: the official vectors at every length up to 102,400 bytes, and big files against the official <code>b3sum</code>. The laws cover what those inputs
    leave out.
  </p>

  {
    lawGroups.map((g) => (
      <div class="group" id={`proofs-${g.id}`}>
        <div class="group-head" data-reveal>
          <h3>{g.title}</h3>
          <p class="prose">{g.blurb}</p>
        </div>
        <ul class:list={['laws', g.cards.length % 3 === 0 ? 'cols-3' : 'cols-2']} role="list">
          {g.cards.map((c, i) => (
            <li class="card law" data-reveal style={`--i: ${i}`}>
              <p class="law-top">
                <span class:list={['badge', `badge-${g.scope}`]}>{badge[g.scope]}</span>
                <span class="names">
                  {c.laws.length > 3 ? (
                    <code>{c.names.join(', ')}</code>
                  ) : (
                    c.laws.map((n) => <code>{n}</code>)
                  )}
                  {c.laws.length > 3 && <span class="n-laws">{c.laws.length} laws</span>}
                </span>
              </p>
              <p class="claim">{powers(c.claim).map((t, i) => (i % 2 === 1 ? <sup>{t}</sup> : t))}</p>
              <p class="covers">{powers(c.covers).map((t, i) => (i % 2 === 1 ? <sup>{t}</sup> : t))}</p>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </div>
    ))
  }

  <div class="how">
    <h3>State it, prove it, check it</h3>
    <ol class="how-steps" role="list">
      <li>
        <p class="how-label"><span class="how-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span> The claim, in <a href={LAWS_URL}>LAWS.bend</a></p>
        <pre><code>{shown.law}</code></pre>
        <p class="how-note">For every input array and every length, the root of the outboard tree is the plain hash.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p class="how-label"><span class="how-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span> The proof, in <a href={PROOF_URL}>PROOF.bend</a></p>
        <pre><code>{shown.proof}</code></pre>
        <p class="how-note">
          A proof is a def. <code>ob.go</code> is an induction over the tree: a recursive call is the induction hypothesis, a <code>match</code> is a case split.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p class="how-label"><span class="how-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span> The gate</p>
        <pre><code><span class="prompt">$</span> bend/prove.sh{'\n'}ALL PROOFS CHECK</code></pre>
        <p class="how-note">
          A false claim does not check: swapping a parent’s children in blake3.bend’s outboard code fails the gate, and so does merging the stream stack’s
          top two the wrong way round.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>

  <aside class="limits" aria-labelledby="proofs-limits">
    <h3 id="proofs-limits">What is not proven</h3>
    <ul role="list">{limits.map((l) => <li>{l}</li>)}</ul>
    <p>
      The laws and proofs are generated by <a href={GENERATOR_URL}>tools/gen_laws.py</a>. <a href={adr('0007').url}>ADR 0007</a>,{' '}
      <a href={adr('0010').url}>ADR 0010</a> and{' '}
      <a href={adr('0015').url}>ADR 0015</a> have how each is proven and what it cost; <a href={blobUrl('bend/prove.sh')}>bend/prove.sh</a> runs the gate.
    </p>
  </aside>
</Section>

<style>
  .stats {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 12rem), 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .stats li {
    display: grid;
    align-content: start;
    gap: 0.35rem;
    padding: 1.1rem 1.25rem;
  }

  .stat {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 1.6rem + 1.6vw, 2.75rem);
    font-weight: 750;
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
    line-height: 1;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }

  .stat-label {
    color: var(--ink-2);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }

  /* Tested vs proven */
  .contrast {
    overflow-x: auto;
  }

  .contrast table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }

  .contrast th,
  .contrast td {
    padding: 0.85rem 1.1rem;
    text-align: left;
    vertical-align: top;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .contrast tbody tr:last-child > * {
    border-bottom: 0;
  }

  .contrast thead th {
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    font-weight: 650;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-3);
  }

  .contrast tbody th {
    font-weight: 650;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .contrast .rust {
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }

  .contrast .bend {
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .law-refs {
    display: inline-flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.3rem;
    margin-left: 0.15em;
  }

  @media (max-width: 40rem) {
    .contrast table,
    .contrast tbody,
    .contrast tr,
    .contrast th,
    .contrast td {
      display: block;
    }

    .contrast thead {
      display: none;
    }

    .contrast tbody tr {
      padding: 0.9rem 1rem;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    }

    .contrast tbody tr:last-child {
      border-bottom: 0;
    }

    .contrast tbody th,
    .contrast td {
      padding: 0;
      border: 0;
      white-space: normal;
    }

    .contrast td {
      margin-top: 0.5rem;
    }

    .contrast td.rust::before {
      content: 'Rust, tested: ';
      font-weight: 650;
      color: var(--ink-3);
    }

    .contrast td.bend::before {
      content: 'Bend2, proven: ';
      font-weight: 650;
      color: var(--ink-3);
    }
  }

  .aside {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }

  /* Law groups */
  .group {
    margin-top: 2.75rem;
  }

  .group-head {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .group-head p {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }

  .laws {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  @media (min-width: 44rem) {
    .laws {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }

  @media (min-width: 64rem) {
    .laws.cols-3 {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }

  .law {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    padding: 1.1rem 1.25rem 1.2rem;
  }

  .law-top {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.4rem 0.6rem;
  }

  .names {
    display: inline-flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.35rem;
  }

  .n-laws {
    color: var(--ink-3);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
  }

  .badge {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0.1rem 0.5rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    border: 1px solid currentColor;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 650;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .badge-every-input {
    color: var(--s-bend);
  }

  .badge-every-size {
    color: var(--s-bend-alt);
  }

  .badge-computed {
    color: var(--ink-3);
  }

  .claim {
    flex: 1;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }

  sup {
    line-height: 0;
  }

  .covers {
    color: var(--ink-3);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }

  /* How */
  .how {
    margin-top: 3rem;
  }

  .how h3 {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .how-steps {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 20rem), 1fr));
    gap: 1.25rem;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .how-steps li {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .how-label {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }

  .how-n {
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    width: 1.6rem;
    height: 1.6rem;
    border-radius: 50%;
    border: 1px solid var(--line-strong);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }

  .how-steps pre {
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
  }

  .prompt {
    color: var(--ink-3);
    user-select: none;
  }

  .how-note {
    color: var(--ink-2);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
  }

  /* Limits */
  .limits {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    margin-top: 2.75rem;
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--axis);
    background: var(--surface-2);
    border-radius: 0 var(--radius-sm) var(--radius-sm) 0;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }

  .limits h3 {
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--ink);
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .limits ul {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
    padding-left: 1.1rem;
  }
</style>
